{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HPEjUHtpsRQ448SmqndKN5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity + R&D mission-control system, built for J.C. Liechty and living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (one folder, plain-markdown source of truth, Python-stdlib-only with one declared `pywinpty` exception).\n\nWhat it is and does:\n\n- **A markdown-backed task/project manager.** It reads and writes plain `.md` files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) as the source of truth â€” tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later, with capture, notes, priorities, and per-domain views (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n\n- **It ships as a persistent local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained stdlib HTTP server that regenerates the full dashboard HTML on every request, bound to `http://localhost:8777` and run as the always-on NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A mirror CLI (`anchor.py`) does the same operations from the command line and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It is also a \"mission-control\" cockpit for AI trio-driven R&D.** Each project gets a window where the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman trio runs as durable, server-side sessions. This is the bulk of recent work (control-surface versions v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4 \"Project Cockpit\", all built and merged to master as of 2026-06-13).\n\n- **The R&D surface provides:** per-lane (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) tiles with one honest status light; real interactive **ConPTY terminals** (xterm.js) isolated in per-session git worktrees; an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini); cached, grounding-validated session/project summaries; cost/tokens/time rollups; stage handoffs; grass-idea promotion; and type-aware deliverable launches (skill/service/program/doc) on guaranteed-non-8777 ports.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file and walking the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, no touching the real `:8777` service or data), writing dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Branding/positioning:** presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\" (vendored brand mark, dashboard favicon, Option-B masthead).\n\nIn short: a one-person, file-based GTD dashboard that has grown an integrated cockpit for running and remembering autonomous AI build/research work."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b9443e7-3812-4c29-9fdb-ca43bad4caec","uuid":"2b6be089-c3d3-45e0-b5b7-12b62469cf56","request_id":"req_011Cc2KKTieuZwHZFv8UnLoM"}
